            <div xml:id="d870">

                <pb facs="0811" n="711" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg711"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">631.6131/187: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Davis</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-05-19T20:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 19, 1920—8
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received May 19—5:42 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>824. My 791, May 14, 6 p.m.<anchor n="99" xml:id="d870-f1"/> I have received an
                    intimation in an entirely unofficial manner that in order to keep our Government
                    informed of developments an invitation may be extended for an American
                    representative to be present at all meetings of the Permanent Committee of the
                    Supreme Economic Council at which the question of Russian trade is discussed. I
                    should welcome an early expression of the Department’s desires should such
                    invitation be received.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Davis</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
